{"id":"22431f6f-8a83-40c6-8744-fca78b049930","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"65301fe6b467afce","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/bridge/capabilities/decide.ts","baseline":{"blob":"9fab26adcc6c91b2d04dadf9eddd15ae76d71065","start":8869,"end":9019},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["async","function","breakGlass","(","request",":","CapabilityRequest",")",":","Promise","<","boolean",">","{","refuseUndecided","(","request",".","scope",",","askerOf","(","request",")",".","package",")",";","return","false",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"39905cc0411dd33c","after":"2eece5664e71e903"}},"payload":{"text":"A redline scope's break-glass: nobody here can authorize one (the shell's prompt went with previews), so it stays\nrefused.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:06.951Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:06.951Z"}
{"id":"303944e9-972d-489a-8939-35bd7fbaa811","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"493e01729b764400","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/bridge/capabilities/decide.ts","baseline":{"blob":"dbeab84eee27d883e5bd5bcbd22385270201bb2b","start":1692,"end":1945},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","interface","CapabilityCall","{","\"","kind","\"",":","\"","net","\"","|","\"","fs","\"","|","\"","exec","\"",";","\"","method","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","op","\"","?",":","\"","read","\"","|","\"","write","\"",";","\"","resource","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","args","\"","?",":","readonly","unknown","[]",";","\"","runId","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","package","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","why","\"","?",":","AskedWhy",";","\"","trigger","\"","?",":","\"","you","\"","|","\"","edit","\"",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"df4b2a20d2eda5da","after":"8d3eca67011b3e0e"}},"payload":{"text":"The RAW call an interceptor sends — deliberately un-classified so the interceptors stay dumb and decoupled\n(almostnode never imports the policy core). Classification happens HERE.\n• net: `{ kind: \"net\", args: [input, init] }` — host derived from the request.\n• fs:  `{ kind: \"fs\", method, args: [path, …] }` — op derived from the method, path from arg 0.\n• exec:`{ kind: \"exec\", args: [command, …] }`.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:47.328Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:47.328Z"}
{"id":"32426783-26a4-48f5-8205-0727d6f4eef9","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"8d3eca67011b3e0e","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/bridge/capabilities/decide.ts","baseline":{"blob":"568a880e69a4e7bcfd38a638009d0f69ea596b3d","start":2990,"end":3198},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["function","packageNamed","(","pkg",":","string",")",":","{","\"","name","\"",":","string",";","\"","version","\"","?",":","string","}","{","const","at","=","pkg",".","lastIndexOf","(","\"","@","\"",")",";","return","at",">","0","?","{","\"","name","\"",":","pkg",".","slice","(","0",",","at",")",",","\"","version","\"",":","pkg",".","slice","(","at","+","1",")","}",":","{","\"","name","\"",":","pkg","}",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"493e01729b764400","after":"b4440802d40c3909"}},"payload":{"text":"A package as `name@version` names it (a scoped name's own `@` kept).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:36.726Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:36.726Z"}
{"id":"39e86597-6e96-4174-b34e-8af9f22712cd","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"5bf3ccd7f078c24b","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/bridge/capabilities/decide.ts","baseline":{"blob":"cdc591ef3122c0b78c7caae1400a733bd7f54ed4","start":10903,"end":10962},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","how",":","{","\"","decided","\"",":","Decided","}","=","{","\"","decided","\"",":","\"","policy","\"","}"]},"context":{"before":"6d60554f303fc147","after":"5443518280bcbf75"}},"payload":{"text":"(an object: the broker's callbacks below set it, which a `let` narrowed to its first value wouldn't show)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:52.456Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:52.456Z"}
{"id":"3e0c0e43-da57-45a7-8691-531a40bf262f","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"924b6c0a8625c617","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/bridge/capabilities/decide.ts","baseline":{"blob":"fab3fff7b1ddb74498c210d416189bfaf8b09929","start":10239,"end":10381},"shape":{"type":"If","atoms":["if","(","call",".","package","!==","undefined",")","{","Object",".","assign","(","request",",","{","\"","package","\"",":","call",".","package","}",",","call",".","why","===","undefined","?","{","}",":","{","\"","why","\"",":","call",".","why","}",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"16f8990f4edf5c8a","after":"c0f7ef4798c94952"}},"payload":{"text":"And whose call it is, and why it's asked: a package's is decided by the rules about its calls.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:58.802Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:58.802Z"}
{"id":"4189853b-2efd-4d5d-a60f-f755e2196fb9","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2914b30ad9f029c0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/bridge/capabilities/decide.ts","baseline":{"blob":"d2f717566a44e20029137cdabf0d23acb14bc2e2","start":4671,"end":4759},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","runAnswers","=","new","Map","<","string",",","{","\"","allowed","\"",":","Set","<","string",">",";","\"","refused","\"",":","Set","<","string",">","}",">","(",")"]},"context":{"before":"8a35768708d6ccfd","after":"6eee3623a3354532"}},"payload":{"text":"Each run's answers at the call: the scopes allowed once — for the rest of that run, never the next — and those\nrefused, not asked again in it. Persisted decisions live in the policy (consulted by the decider), not here.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:28.340Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:28.340Z"}
{"id":"434e0799-5988-4a36-944e-1577541e28c9","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"fa958ac3f6e98a78","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/bridge/capabilities/decide.ts","baseline":{"blob":"7639e393569ffd3e37e28bcee16cbe39c285b9ba","start":6646,"end":7024},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["function","refuseUndecided","(","scope",":","string",",","pkg",":","string","|","undefined",")",":","void","{","if","(","!","undecidedSaid",".","has","(","scope",")",")","{","undecidedSaid",".","add","(","scope",")",";","void","vscode",".","window",".","showWarningMessage","(","`","","${","pkg","===","undefined","?","\"","A call","\"",":","`","","${","pkg","}","'s call","`","}"," to ","${","scope","}"," wasn't made: the policy doesn't decide it, and nothing here asks yet. Allow it with a rule in your policy (.silo/policy/<you>.json).","`",")",";","}","}"]},"context":{"before":"e0d9ee90980533a3","after":"39905cc0411dd33c"}},"payload":{"text":"An undecided call, refused — and said, once a scope: nothing in the core asks a person at the call yet (the\nshell's prompt went with previews), so the policy decides, and what it leaves undecided isn't made.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:15.478Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:15.478Z"}
